rule cs1:
x is a rel3 if
    x is a rel1
    and x is a rel2
    and it is not the case that the statement cs2 applies.

% Blah blah.
rule ps1:
x is not a rel3 if
    x is a rel1
    and x is a rel2
        or x is a rel2.

% defeater cs2: it concludes nothing; the rules whose conclusion it attacks do not apply when it does
the statement cs2 applies if
    x is a rel1
    and x is a rel2.

% defeater ps2: an exception of the rules whose conclusion it attacks
scenario both_conditions is:
    x is a rel1.
    x is a rel2.
    not_rel3 expects answers ["x is not a rel3"].
    rel3 expects answers [].

scenario one_condition is:
    x is a rel1.
    not_rel3 expects answers [].
    rel3 expects answers [].

query not_rel3 is:
    which thing is not a rel3.

query rel3 is:
    which thing is a rel3.

